Z||000002||lowCG||07-17-2000||06:26 PM||||I'm using a West Coast Fiero disc,and a Luk,oem Fiero replacement pressure plate on my 3400TDC,feels great,real smooth,but I haven't thrashed on it yet.The discs are supposed to last around 30,000+,depending on how it's treated.It's a Kevlar material,that's supposed to grab harder when heated,like a race brake pad.<BR>I bought mine from them because they actually own and drive these cars,where most clutch rebuilders wanted to over-do the pressure plate,and I didn't want to stress the clutch release setup.||||reg||1
Z||000003||HYPTNOTiSE||07-18-2000||05:24 PM||||Mine from Clutchnet cost me 315, with a pressure plate and disk, 40,000 mile waranty and an upgraded pressure plate over stock. 2100psi. <P><P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000004||PJ||07-19-2000||10:21 PM||||I've wiped out the stock type organic disks in short order, but I'm road racing the car. Switched to a kevlar disk which works very well but now the Luk pressure plate that comes with it is the weak link. You won't know what the weak component is 'till you go in and look.<P><BR>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black||||reg||1
